    "value": "No — Texas's felony-disqualification requirement (Tex. Elec. Code § 141.001(a)(4)) applies only to \"a public elective office in this state\" by its own text, not federal office; separately, the U.S. Constitution's own qualifications for Congress (age, citizenship, residency) can't be added to by any state, so this doesn't reach U.S. House or Senate candidates either way",
